OL,3,GNEWSA'Who will pay the costs of paused
OL,4,Acouncil shake-up?'
OL,5,
OL,6,FWhat will come next for Devon after a
OL,7,Fsurprise announcement by the government
OL,8,Fto "pause" plans for the biggest
OL,9,Fshake-up of local government for more
OL,10,Fthan 50 years?
OL,12,FThe plan approved by the government was
OL,13,Fto abolish all the district, county and
OL,14,Funitary councils in Devon and replace
OL,15,Fthem with four new unitary councils -
OL,16,Fwith Plymouth, Torbay and Exeter all
OL,17,Fexpanding.
OL,23,APub: 13-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
FL,347,340,200,160,0,100
PN,34602
SC,0002
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F346A1789280815
OL,1,W5j 5Q555pjsjjj js17kjc15 js57kj#4
OL,2,W//%*// //%Q--% (.*.. *,$%**,%-,* %%**,!
OL,3,GNEWSA'Who will pay the costs of paused
OL,4,Acouncil shake-up?'
OL,5,
OL,6,FAccording to the architects of that
OL,7,Fplan - the Labour leaders of Plymouth
OL,8,Fand Exeter - the "pause" by the
OL,9,Fgovernment is a delay that is
OL,10,Fworthwhile to "get it right".
OL,12,FBut the leader of Devon County Council
OL,13,Fbelieves the scheme is "cancelled" and
OL,14,Fwants compensation from the government
OL,15,Ffor the time and money it has already
OL,16,Fspent.
OL,23,APub: 13-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG2/2
